# Profiles module boundary

- Code under `modules/profiles/**` must never import directly from
  `modules/users/src/**`. If profile logic needs user data, reference it
  through `modules/shared/src/**` or an HTTP call - never a direct
  source import across the module line.
- Any change to `modules/profiles/src/validators/profiles.validator.ts`
  must be accompanied by a test in `modules/profiles/tests/**` covering
  both an accepted and a rejected case for the specific rule changed.
- Postal-code validation must account for `country` - never apply a
  single hard-coded regex to every country. This is a known area of
  risk in this module; treat any postal-code validation change as
  security/correctness sensitive and request a narrow, reviewable diff.
- Follow the existing pattern in this module: routes wire paths only,
  controllers hold logic, validators are separate middleware, `sendError`
  from `@shared/utils/http` is the only way to return an error body.
